racist rants by federal land moocher  cliven Bundy and vile comments  attributed to Los Angeles Clippers owner  Donald sterling and put old-school  racism back in the news but let's get  real  however contemptible Bundy and sterling  aren't what's holding down blacks and  other minorities in today's America  here are three policies that whatever  their original intentions systematically  screw over poor blacks and other  minorities whether it's absurd licensing  laws for at-home hair braiders day care  operators and other small-time  entrepreneurs or minimum wage laws that  price young unskilled black kids out of  their first jobs barriers to the labor  market take their biggest hole on those  with the least education skills and  professional connections created amidst  fears of cocaine snorting Negros opium  smoking Chinese and pot puffing Mexicans  the drug war not only locks up blacks  and minorities in vastly unfair and  unjustifiable numbers  it also concentrates black-market  violence in poor urban neighborhoods  blacks don't use drugs more than whites  they just pay a much steeper price  despite more than doubling real  per-pupil expenditures since the early  1970s  America's graduating high school seniors  have shown no meaningful improvements in  math reading and science it's black and  Hispanic kids in inner cities whose  parents lack any real choice in schools  that suffer the most and yet politicians  teachers and parents who can afford to  exercise choice for their own kids do  everything they can to keep poor kids  trapped in failing schools at a combined  140 years old Bundy and sterling are  survivors from an older uglier America  that died well before the election of  Barack Obama they can go for themselves  but if the rest of us actually want to  address the sort of racism that's  screwing over today's minorities we'd do  better to bust down barriers to work and  the drug war and tear apart the school  monopoly for Reason TV I'm Nicholas
 

